abstract: This Lean 4/mathlib library develops a common generating source into natural-number
  arithmetic, finite expression histories and basic physical response structures. Its arithmetic
  branch retains how a value is generated, then proves that retained history differences can
  affect later value response. Its physical branch constructs gauge and matter data and proves
  the generated Yang-Mills action, complete differential Hessian and attained positive spectral
  gap in the specified source model.
